WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.080
Which is better for a refactor,

2
00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:04.267
Claude Code or Gemini CLI?

3
00:00:04.267 --> 00:00:07.407
I don't have evidence for a universal winner,

4
00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:12.167
so I'd compare how each tool shows you its plan and its failures.

5
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:16.600
Claude Code lets you review its plan or approve sensitive tool calls first,

6
00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:19.633
which matters when a refactor crosses several files.

7
00:00:19.633 --> 00:00:23.093
Gemini CLI also supports an edit-and-verify loop,

8
00:00:23.093 --> 00:00:25.253
but automation isn't proof,

9
00:00:25.253 --> 00:00:28.233
so it depends on whether your checks catch the failures.

10
00:00:28.233 --> 00:00:32.173
So I'd run both on the same task and commit,

11
00:00:32.173 --> 00:00:36.313
and judge their patches with the same tests before picking a winner.
